    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: *when more than 80 owners have already been created today, the owner response includes `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`.* The acceptance test reads the flag back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so it needed to be a response field on every `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` conversion, not just on create.\n\nI kept each piece of logic in its natural home and reused what already existed:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` read-only boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field (matching how all other derived fields like `locality`/`membershipTier` are declared).\n\n2. **`BulkSignupWarningEvaluator`** (new, in `rest.validation`) \u2014 a small single-responsibility component that answers *\"has today exceeded the warning threshold?\"*. It **reuses the existing `DailyRegistrationCounter`** (the same by-registration-date accumulation path the per-day cap uses, as the test comment notes) rather than re-counting, and defines its own `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` (`count > 80`), kept separate from the unrelated `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100` cap.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 converted from an interface to an abstract MapStruct mapper (still `componentModel=spring`) with the evaluator injected, and an `@AfterMapping` hook that stamps the flag onto every mapped `OwnerDto`. This is the single point where `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` derivation happens, so create, `getOwner`, `listOwners`, and the paged endpoint all get consistent behavior without duplicating logic into controllers.\n\nThe flag is response-evaluated (not persisted), which is correct since it depends on the day's global registration volume rather than any stored owner field.\n\nFull test suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1/1 passing.",
